Document the SizedLength() class in the latex documentation.
Note that I intend to start using it for length-encoded
stuff in the near future (especially strings and STL
containers).  This will invalidate data I have on disk,
but I can live with that (I think).

Look at what will be affected by moving to SizedLength()
for string and STL containers.  What will be adversely affected
in my home?  mcblockd, sitetrafficd, sitehealthd, etc.

Look at splitting the library apart.  I'd like a separate
libDwmIO library focused on I/O, a separate libDwmSyslog
for SysLogger, and probably a separate libDwmUnitAssert.
Then what do I do with the rest?
